WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:11.270 --> 00:13.530
It might be inappropriate

3
00:11.360 --> 00:16.030
[It might be inappropriate of me to say this when I made a mistake yesterday...]

4
00:13.660 --> 00:15.780
of me to say this when I made a mistake yesterday...

5
00:15.780 --> 00:17.820
But can you promise me one thing?

6
00:16.059 --> 00:18.290
[But can you promise me one thing?]

7
00:19.320 --> 00:20.420
What?

8
00:23.990 --> 00:27.240
[No matter what happens in the future, don't get hurt, you fool.]

9
00:24.010 --> 00:26.430
No matter what happens in the future, don't get hurt,

10
00:26.430 --> 00:27.500
you fool.

11
00:32.650 --> 00:34.200
[Promise me.]

12
00:32.800 --> 00:33.950
Promise me.

13
00:39.900 --> 00:41.220
I promise you.

14
00:42.850 --> 00:44.750
As long as you stay by my side,

15
00:45.200 --> 00:47.640
I won't let anyone get hurt.

16
00:48.420 --> 00:49.500
Promise.

17
00:54.890 --> 00:55.930
But

18
00:57.370 --> 00:59.970
you're already covered in scars because of me.

19
01:13.789 --> 01:20.370
[Some scenes were created with AI.]

20
01:22.600 --> 01:26.320
[Adapted from the webtoon "The Sound of Sugar Cubes" by Kim Tak]

21
01:26.320 --> 01:29.110
[Screenwriter: So-on (JD)]

22
01:29.120 --> 01:32.020
[Director: Yoon Jinyoung]

23
01:48.520 --> 01:50.220
[Yoo Dohyun]

24
01:50.360 --> 01:51.680
[Cho Chanhyeon]

25
01:51.800 --> 01:53.370
[Ko Gyeol]

26
01:55.180 --> 01:58.360
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

27
02:03.920 --> 02:04.950
Hanyul.

28
02:07.880 --> 02:08.889
Here.

29
02:09.300 --> 02:11.980
This is a wild river eel found only deep in Jirisan.

30
02:11.980 --> 02:13.570
I heard you have to boil it without anything to get a thick broth,

31
02:13.570 --> 02:14.900
so I put the whole eel in.

32
02:15.070 --> 02:16.540
Try it.

33
02:17.280 --> 02:18.950
Ah, is it too big?

34
02:19.540 --> 02:21.040
I'll cut it up for you.

35
02:29.290 --> 02:32.950
This is bat bile found only in the high mountains of the Himalayas.

36
02:36.540 --> 02:37.710
So bitter.

37
02:44.829 --> 02:45.760
Damn it.

38
02:45.950 --> 02:47.240
What are you doing?

39
02:47.360 --> 02:49.140
Hey, fire! Fire!

40
02:49.260 --> 02:50.610
Fire! Fire...

41
02:52.130 --> 02:54.560
Water! It's a flood! Damn it!

42
02:54.570 --> 02:56.210
Seriously, Lee Won?

43
03:12.680 --> 03:14.090
I originally wanted to

44
03:14.530 --> 03:16.350
just build a fountain,

45
03:16.470 --> 03:18.750
but I was afraid of being scolded by Pan, so I held it back.

46
03:18.750 --> 03:21.300
They say you have to sleep in a humid environment

47
03:21.300 --> 03:24.160
so your vocal cords can recover as soon as possible.

48
03:25.140 --> 03:26.210
Come on.

49
03:26.700 --> 03:27.940
Make a wish quickly.

50
03:29.120 --> 03:33.170
Please let Lee Hanyul's voice recover as soon as possible.

51
03:34.850 --> 03:37.090
Hey, you make a wish too.

52
03:39.170 --> 03:42.000
Hey, why aren't you making a wish?

53
03:44.700 --> 03:45.750
Ah.

54
03:46.210 --> 03:47.530
You can't speak.

55
03:48.210 --> 03:49.610
Are you stupid?

56
03:51.120 --> 03:53.590
Yeah, I am stupid.

57
03:54.990 --> 03:57.770
So until your voice goes back to normal,

58
03:57.920 --> 03:59.810
I'll continue to be stupid.

59
04:01.590 --> 04:02.750
Make a wish.

60
04:27.090 --> 04:28.290
What! What happened!

61
04:28.440 --> 04:30.500
Damn it, who is it!

62
04:30.760 --> 04:32.530
What is all this?

63
04:33.020 --> 04:34.680
I heard this is the best for reducing swelling,

64
04:34.680 --> 04:36.850
so I took a bath with the highest grade herbal concentrate.

65
04:36.850 --> 04:38.550
Maybe there's a hole in the tub.

66
04:38.550 --> 04:40.350
I was taking a half-body bath...

67
04:40.600 --> 04:42.070
You, wait a minute.

68
04:42.080 --> 04:44.200
I thought you were dead!

69
04:44.320 --> 04:45.130
Hey.

70
04:45.300 --> 04:47.060
Hanyul, you... you spoke!

71
04:47.370 --> 04:48.070
Oh?

72
04:50.210 --> 04:50.920
You spoke!

73
04:51.030 --> 04:51.740
I spoke!

74
04:51.870 --> 04:52.870
You spoke!

75
04:53.110 --> 04:54.100
-You spoke! -I spoke!

76
04:54.100 --> 04:57.090
You spoke! You have a voice!

77
04:59.120 --> 05:00.320
Ah, ah.

78
05:01.400 --> 05:03.460
But it's really a blessing, isn't it?

79
05:04.130 --> 05:05.020
Hey.

80
05:06.750 --> 05:09.270
Lee Won has done so much for you.

81
05:09.430 --> 05:11.000
With his sincerity,

82
05:11.110 --> 05:13.970
even the carrots in the fridge might start talking.

83
05:15.800 --> 05:18.650
I'm suddenly curious if carrots can talk.

84
05:18.900 --> 05:20.710
You just want to eat carrots, don't you?

85
05:20.710 --> 05:21.670
Yeah.

86
05:28.610 --> 05:31.710
[Lee Won, I hope your voice recovers soon. I have something I really want to give you.]

87
05:32.159 --> 05:33.690
By the way, where is Lee Won?

88
05:34.720 --> 05:36.510
Secretary Kim said

89
05:36.670 --> 05:40.020
he hasn't been to work for days and has been holed up in his room.

90
05:40.020 --> 05:41.440
Could he be composing?

91
05:45.830 --> 05:52.350
[My voice is...]

92
05:53.500 --> 05:54.690
I'm going out for a bit.

93
05:54.690 --> 05:56.520
Hey, finish eating before you go.

94
05:56.520 --> 05:57.420
Hey!

95
05:57.680 --> 05:59.010
You're leaving them...

96
06:00.980 --> 06:02.030
Oh.

97
06:02.240 --> 06:03.420
You're here.

98
06:03.900 --> 06:05.890
I was just about to go look for you.

99
06:09.050 --> 06:09.760
Here.

100
06:09.930 --> 06:10.940
It's yours.

101
06:14.230 --> 06:15.960
I finally finished writing it.

102
06:16.160 --> 06:17.530
A song for you.

103
06:19.580 --> 06:20.970
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

104
06:21.300 --> 06:22.300
Oh.

105
06:23.070 --> 06:24.790
Why did you come to my house?

106
06:25.520 --> 06:27.630
I can speak now.

107
06:29.810 --> 06:30.920
Seriously?

108
06:31.080 --> 06:31.730
Yeah.

109
06:31.860 --> 06:32.760
Listen.

110
06:34.080 --> 06:37.370
Lee Won, I can speak now!

111
06:42.930 --> 06:44.260
That's great.

112
06:45.060 --> 06:46.700
That's really great.

113
06:55.850 --> 06:58.750
By the way, what is this? Mine?

114
06:59.050 --> 07:00.980
Yeah, yours.

115
07:06.650 --> 07:08.550
You need to warm up your voice first.

116
07:08.550 --> 07:10.810
After all, you haven't used it in a while.

117
07:10.940 --> 07:14.490
Okay, let's go to the piano...

118
07:17.280 --> 07:19.280
What are you doing in broad daylight?

119
07:19.280 --> 07:21.670
What else? Practicing scales.

120
07:21.970 --> 07:23.390
Here?

121
07:23.780 --> 07:25.610
There's an instrument here,

122
07:25.780 --> 07:27.510
and I'm in charge of playing it.

123
07:29.610 --> 07:31.070
Do you need anything else?

124
07:31.160 --> 07:33.220
What nonsense are you talking about?

125
08:04.590 --> 08:07.200
So don't hold back your voice, Hanyul.

126
08:20.080 --> 08:21.880
I've already warmed up my voice.

127
08:21.930 --> 08:23.020
Let's stop here.

128
08:25.370 --> 08:26.520
By the way,

129
08:27.000 --> 08:28.930
why did you suddenly give me a song?

130
08:31.370 --> 08:32.929
-Could it be... -Yeah.

131
08:33.720 --> 08:34.980
You're going to debut.

132
08:35.039 --> 08:36.370
Really?

133
08:46.340 --> 08:49.830
[Park Hanhoo's Manager]

134
08:52.370 --> 08:56.370
[Park Hanhoo's Manager] [The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

135
09:08.740 --> 09:11.440
[Park Hanhoo's Manager]

136
09:19.890 --> 09:22.790
Who could be so good at vocal training?

137
09:24.020 --> 09:27.380
I truly... admire myself too.

138
09:40.290 --> 09:43.490
Judas's "Afternoon Rock and Roll."

139
09:43.600 --> 09:45.410
Today's special surprise guest is

140
09:45.410 --> 09:50.150
the one sweeping the national music charts.

141
09:50.480 --> 09:53.230
Singing the OST for "Park Hanhoo's Manager,"

142
09:53.350 --> 09:57.180
the eardrum boyfriend whose heavenly voice melts the public's eardrums—

143
09:57.180 --> 09:59.040
is Yul!

144
10:01.630 --> 10:03.760
We really had a hard time inviting him.

145
10:03.830 --> 10:06.630
The listener message board has already exploded.

146
10:06.860 --> 10:10.590
Yeah, just hearing his voice makes you think he must be super handsome.

147
10:10.590 --> 10:13.700
Even though he's a faceless singer, it feels like you can see his face.

148
10:13.700 --> 10:17.680
We can see him right now.

149
10:17.930 --> 10:19.410
Are you all jealous?

150
10:19.550 --> 10:22.730
I should say, just looking at him makes you feel very satisfied.

151
10:22.730 --> 10:24.590
Did you give birth to him, Samuel?

152
10:24.700 --> 10:26.810
Yeah, I even want to say I gave birth to him.

153
10:26.810 --> 10:29.720
In my opinion, if you say you gave birth to him,

154
10:29.840 --> 10:33.200
there's absolutely no resemblance in appearance.

155
10:33.330 --> 10:35.010
Alright, enough with the jokes.

156
10:35.010 --> 10:37.720
Yul, you debuted as a faceless singer.

157
10:37.850 --> 10:41.320
Is there any special reason you chose not to reveal your face?

158
10:42.590 --> 10:47.010
I just hope the public can hear my voice first.

159
10:47.460 --> 10:50.390
I just want to keep everyone company with my singing.

160
10:50.910 --> 10:54.140
We actually want to focus more on your face.

161
10:54.630 --> 10:57.190
We just want to focus on your face.

162
10:57.550 --> 10:58.760
Well.

163
10:58.880 --> 11:02.290
Then I'll start asking the question everyone's most curious about.

164
11:02.290 --> 11:06.770
We heard you didn't do music before, but worked in other industries.

165
11:06.920 --> 11:11.150
So what was the reason, and how did you get the chance to sing this song?

166
11:17.140 --> 11:18.540
-Really? -Yeah.

167
11:18.700 --> 11:21.110
Hanyul, thank you for your hard work today.

168
11:21.330 --> 11:22.610
Thank you for coming to my show.

169
11:22.610 --> 11:23.850
-Thank you. -You really did a great job.

170
11:23.850 --> 11:25.510
We have things to wrap up,

171
11:25.640 --> 11:27.350
so we'll only leave later.

172
11:27.570 --> 11:28.320
Thank you.

173
11:28.430 --> 11:29.340
-Good job. -Take care.

174
11:29.340 --> 11:30.550
Thank you.

175
11:30.690 --> 11:31.600
Take care.

176
11:38.980 --> 11:40.640
Aren't you a faceless singer?

177
11:44.700 --> 11:47.950
You contacted Dawn Entertainment, right?

178
11:49.000 --> 11:51.910
You know Pan and Michelo don't get along,

179
11:52.310 --> 11:54.010
so you wanted to mess with us.

180
11:54.790 --> 11:57.320
I'm not quite sure what you're talking about.

181
11:57.630 --> 12:02.280
I don't know either Pan or Michelo.

182
12:02.930 --> 12:05.140
I just want you to become popular as soon as possible.

183
12:05.140 --> 12:06.270
You don't know them?

184
12:07.570 --> 12:08.740
Really?

185
12:09.240 --> 12:10.100
Yeah.

186
12:11.560 --> 12:14.100
You really are easily misunderstood.

187
12:15.260 --> 12:17.860
You had nothing to do with Dawn Entertainment.

188
12:18.560 --> 12:21.020
And you had nothing to do with Adolph either.

189
12:23.500 --> 12:25.390
You must feel very wronged.

190
12:26.440 --> 12:27.510
Right?

191
12:29.960 --> 12:33.290
Lee Hanyul, how many times do I have to say this?

192
12:33.420 --> 12:35.670
I really didn't kill Adolph.

193
12:37.760 --> 12:38.970
Really?

194
12:39.600 --> 12:40.770
I guess.

195
12:44.410 --> 12:45.560
Adolph

196
12:48.670 --> 12:49.990
is still alive.

197
12:56.850 --> 13:00.810
I didn't dare let you see Adolph who won't wake up.

198
13:01.430 --> 13:04.620
But I thought if I kept him this way,

199
13:07.880 --> 13:10.570
you might look at me differently.

200
13:15.760 --> 13:18.240
I did have evil thoughts.

201
13:20.990 --> 13:22.360
But I...

202
13:29.580 --> 13:30.630
What's wrong?

203
13:31.960 --> 13:33.390
Adolph...

204
13:33.900 --> 13:35.100
is gone.

205
13:35.300 --> 13:36.400
What did you say?

206
13:41.810 --> 13:43.040
It's true!

207
13:43.180 --> 13:45.240
I really have been taking care of him!

208
13:45.560 --> 13:47.740
Why on earth do you have to go this far?

209
13:48.370 --> 13:50.100
Using the excuse of Adolph who's dead—

210
13:50.100 --> 13:52.030
what exactly do you want to do to me?

211
13:52.870 --> 13:54.610
Will you only stop when you see me dead?

212
13:54.610 --> 13:55.690
Is that it?

213
14:05.480 --> 14:07.270
Adolph is not dead.

214
14:07.390 --> 14:09.790
I thought when he wakes up, I'll find you...

215
14:11.530 --> 14:12.500
Here.

216
14:14.730 --> 14:16.000
Are you satisfied now?

217
14:16.410 --> 14:19.770
You didn't just kill Adolph that day.

218
14:20.070 --> 14:22.030
You killed me too.

219
14:28.400 --> 14:29.470
Who are you?

220
14:33.070 --> 14:34.340
Just kill me.

221
14:34.470 --> 14:36.200
I'm telling you to just kill me!

222
14:47.470 --> 14:49.940
[Sound of Dawn]

223
14:59.850 --> 15:00.940
Hanyul!

224
15:05.100 --> 15:07.760
I was planning to have a beer alone. Want to join?

225
15:07.800 --> 15:08.640
Sure.

226
15:10.180 --> 15:12.670
How does it feel to officially debut?

227
15:13.630 --> 15:14.870
Just so-so.

228
15:15.210 --> 15:16.290
You must be a little dazed.

229
15:16.290 --> 15:18.550
With the sudden surge in popularity too.

230
15:19.780 --> 15:21.730
I just wonder if I'm qualified enough.

231
15:21.730 --> 15:23.810
Huh? Why?

232
15:23.940 --> 15:28.370
You absolutely deserve to be loved.

233
15:29.470 --> 15:31.430
I might not be a good person.

234
15:32.090 --> 15:35.650
No one is perfect from beginning to end.

235
15:35.780 --> 15:38.850
Everyone has a little bit of badness in them.

236
15:39.470 --> 15:43.050
Instead, those who claim to be super nice people

237
15:43.180 --> 15:45.310
are the ones you should be more wary of.

238
15:47.630 --> 15:48.650
Oh, right.

239
15:48.850 --> 15:52.770
I heard you and Herod have been good friends since high school.

240
15:53.460 --> 15:58.360
Just now, I could tell he seems to like you a lot.

241
16:06.310 --> 16:11.290
Seems like he must've done something gravely wrong to you.

242
16:13.900 --> 16:15.750
But, Hanyul,

243
16:15.920 --> 16:19.350
although I don't know what exactly it is,

244
16:19.680 --> 16:22.720
he probably didn't have any bad intentions.

245
16:23.100 --> 16:28.730
He is indeed selfish and values his own feelings the most in the world.

246
16:33.720 --> 16:36.260
Actually, all of us members

247
16:36.510 --> 16:39.690
owe him our lives.

248
16:41.790 --> 16:43.020
Owe him?

249
16:45.630 --> 16:49.030
Back then, Saul's family was in a bad financial situation,

250
16:49.380 --> 16:51.620
and he got involved with a bunch of shady jerks

251
16:51.620 --> 16:53.640
and became completely depraved.

252
16:53.840 --> 16:56.000
The one who risked his life to get him out,

253
16:56.000 --> 16:57.910
paid for his medical treatment, and made him a decent person,

254
16:57.910 --> 16:59.070
was Herod.

255
17:00.290 --> 17:02.780
The one who helped Samuel's family pay off their debts

256
17:02.780 --> 17:05.839
and let him pick up the drumsticks again was also Herod.

257
17:06.589 --> 17:10.280
As for me, when I had nowhere

258
17:10.400 --> 17:12.660
and was wandering around on the Han River Bridge,

259
17:12.660 --> 17:15.800
he grabbed me by the collar and pulled me down.

260
17:16.280 --> 17:21.339
In other people's eyes, he might be a cold-blooded bastard,

261
17:21.640 --> 17:25.819
but to us, he is our only salvation.

262
17:27.099 --> 17:31.090
He did so much, yet never mentioned his own difficulties.

263
17:31.230 --> 17:32.800
He's just a fool.

264
17:34.210 --> 17:35.980
Anyway, what I mean is,

265
17:36.120 --> 17:38.170
what he did to you

266
17:38.290 --> 17:40.740
might look like a mess at first glance,

267
17:41.080 --> 17:43.620
but deep down, it probably isn't like that.

268
17:48.690 --> 17:51.360
I don't even know what happened between you two,

269
17:51.500 --> 17:53.470
and here I am rambling off.

270
17:53.600 --> 17:57.060
I'm sorry for saying all this when I don't even know your story.

271
17:57.190 --> 17:58.460
It's okay.

272
17:58.580 --> 18:00.350
Thank you for telling me this.

273
18:01.420 --> 18:03.510
Shall we toast?

274
18:03.880 --> 18:08.140
When we make our comeback, the top spot on the music charts will be ours again.

275
18:30.030 --> 18:32.930
[You did well today.]

276
18:32.990 --> 18:36.490
[Secretary, you might need to see this.]

277
18:37.010 --> 18:39.390
[The real reason why rookie singer Yul debuted without showing his face (Goosebumps inducing)] [I heard he was involved in a friend's disappearance case in high school?]

278
18:39.510 --> 18:41.490
[The dirty private life of rookie singer Yul]

279
18:41.700 --> 18:43.720
[In this day and age, there are actually singers who make their debut by selling their bodies, haha]

280
18:43.870 --> 18:45.530
[Hot posts related to Yul]

281
18:45.670 --> 18:47.300
[In this day and age, there are actually singers who make their debut by selling their bodies, haha]

282
18:47.440 --> 18:50.940
[Faceless singer Yul's involvement in a missing persons case causes a huge stir]

283
18:52.740 --> 18:56.440
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]
